Subject: Do not resolve the default listen address where ListenAddress lines wait
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Werewolf refuses netlink to sshd's processes]
Reference: werewolf docs/design/ssh-hardening.md

sshd-session parses its configuration with reexec set, which leaves the
ListenAddress lines queued and unresolved, and fill_default_server_options
then resolves the default, every address of every family, for each
connection. sshd-session never listens. glibc sorts that two-address result
by asking netlink, which Werewolf's pledge for sshd refuses, so every
connection logged a refused socket(AF_NETLINK). The listener resolves its
queue before filling defaults, so it is unchanged.

diff --git a/servconf.c b/servconf.c
--- a/servconf.c
+++ b/servconf.c
@@ -338,7 +338,8 @@
 	/* No certificates by default */
 	if (options->num_ports == 0)
 		options->ports[options->num_ports++] = SSH_DEFAULT_PORT;
-	if (options->listen_addrs == NULL)
+	/* sshd-session keeps the ListenAddress lines it never binds queued */
+	if (options->listen_addrs == NULL && options->num_queued_listens == 0)
 		add_listen_addr(options, NULL, NULL, 0);
 	if (options->pid_file == NULL)
 		options->pid_file = xstrdup(_PATH_SSH_DAEMON_PID_FILE);
